          "q": "Is an accumulating UCITS fund taxed every year?",
          "a": "<p>The usual working position is that no dividend income arises until units are sold, because nothing is paid to the investor. This is a reading of the receipt and accrual rules, not an express exemption, so the fund's terms should be checked. The gain is taxed when the units are sold.</p>"
